	file.0000000000000001.title: "Create Energistics"
	quest.00611844AFD5C31E.quest_desc: [
		"While the Inscriber and Charger will natively accept RF/FE, the vast majority of an ME network uses its own dedicated power system called AE."
		""
		"RF/FE can be converted into the native AE at a ratio of 2:1 RF:AE, either directly through an ME Controller, or through the &bEnergy Acceptor&f, which can instead be connected to any part of the network."
	]
	quest.00611844AFD5C31E.quest_subtitle: "energy conversion"
	quest.0081604AF08D98A2.quest_desc: [
		"The &6large water wheel&r works the same as the regular water wheel but has a few differences, it will spin slower than a &eregular water wheel&r but it can will produce a higher stress capacity before it stops from over stressing. It also doesn't matter if 1 or more sides are covered as it will produce the same amount of stress units"
		""
		"It can also be aesthetically changed to match any plank type you right click on it"
	]
	quest.0081604AF08D98A2.quest_subtitle: "Bigger but slower"
	quest.00D06DB43DB3EECB.quest_subtitle: "Connect this to your Energy Source to teleport energy wherever you want"
	quest.00D06DB43DB3EECB.title: "Wireless Connections"
	quest.0125799CA778E1F4.quest_desc: ["A &6gearbox&r is used to change the direction of rotation"]
	quest.0125799CA778E1F4.quest_subtitle: "You can craft each gearbox into the other one"
	quest.01F3F0C25BA72BDA.quest_desc: [
		"Aside from the storage of items and fluids, AE2 also provides a native way of storing entire &estructures&f inside of storage cells, not too dissimilarly to the Compact Machines mod."
		""
		"The &bSpatial IO Port&f allows structures contained within a &bSpatial Containment Structure&f to be captured within a specially-designed storage cell, activated via a redstone signal."
		""
		"If a mob or player happens to stand inside of the SCS while the space is being captured, they too will be transported to where the rest of the space goes, i.e. in a dedicated dimension. Just make sure you have a way to get back out and in if you're the one being captured."
	]
	quest.01F3F0C25BA72BDA.title: "Spatial IO"
	quest.0228747D6C21928F.quest_subtitle: "Make a hoe"
	quest.0228747D6C21928F.title: "Farming away"
	quest.029007D8E8446038.quest_desc: ["The &6train track&r is the thing that the train need to be assembled on and that they run on. They are integral for a train system to work"]
	quest.029007D8E8446038.quest_subtitle: "The key to train travel"
	quest.02EA7BD1BE0587EA.title: "basic energy storage upgrade I"
	quest.02FDDF872A9667BA.quest_desc: ["The &6chute&r acts similar to a hopper and dropper combined, as you can stack them on top of eachother and they will continue to funnnel the items down and drop them once they reach the end but they can also push items up if there is an &6encased fan&r blowing air up through the &6chute&r"]
	quest.02FDDF872A9667BA.quest_subtitle: "A way to move items"
	quest.02FE61BB85143811.quest_desc: [
		"The &6weighted ejector&r let's you send items through the air. "
		"To select the place that the &6ejector&r will send to, you shift right click the block you want it to land on then you can place the &6ejector&r down where you want the items to be flung from."
		""
		"You can edit the weight of the &6ejector&r, to do that you find an x on the &6ejector&r then hold right click whilst looking at it and then move the scroll wheel that appears to the amount of items that you want to be on the &6ejector&r"
	]
	quest.02FE61BB85143811.quest_subtitle: "Fling Items through the air"
	quest.035D8D1D349F7BC3.title: "Enter an &6Ancient City&r"
	quest.037488EF1F3581CE.quest_desc: [
		"By default, an ME network on its own only has an internal buffer of 800AE without an ME Controller, with the controller adding an extra 8kAE per block. For large enough networks, this can be insufficient and may cause a network to power off intermittently when trying to recoup power for any connected devices."
		""
		"The &bEnergy Cell&f allows for an ME network to hold significantly more energy, adding another 200kAE per regular Energy Cell and 1.6MAE per &bDense&f Energy Cell. These can also be placed anywhere in the network to provide the increased energy buffer."
	]
	quest.037488EF1F3581CE.quest_subtitle: "energy storage"
	quest.03C063D04037EEA7.quest_desc: ["Create has a feature built into it called &6Ponder&r, you can hold W on any create item and when the bar fills you will get shown how you can use the item in the world"]
	quest.03C063D04037EEA7.quest_subtitle: "Click the tick to start learning"
	quest.03E500405A6CA1FB.quest_desc: ["The &6half drawers&r hold half of their respective full sized drawers"]
	quest.03E500405A6CA1FB.quest_subtitle: "What it holds"
	quest.03E6FA4DCB71162E.quest_desc: [
		"The &bColor Applicator&f is a chargeable tool that allows for in-world dyeing of cables. It functions more or less as a specialised &estorage cell&f to be loaded up with either vanilla dyes or &epaint balls&f for specific colours, along with &esnowballs&f to wash colours off and turn cables back to their Fluix variant."
		""
		"Applying colour to a cable uses 100AE of energy from its internal battery, for a total of 3400 cable segments in a single charge."
	]
	quest.03E6FA4DCB71162E.title: "Color Applicator"
	quest.03E84F6F607B0C2A.quest_desc: ["This works if cheats are enabled. If you dont have them enabled, temorarily enable them before claiming this quest"]
	quest.03E86E01D0D37F26.quest_subtitle: "used for installing upgrades on the &fmekasuit&r and &fmeka-tool&r"
	quest.04204B276392D733.quest_subtitle: "power movement"
	quest.0420DD4A8BB3868F.quest_desc: ["The &6mechanical arm&r can be setup to move items from one spot to another spot like depot to depot"]
	quest.0420DD4A8BB3868F.quest_subtitle: "A helping hand"
	quest.043768F941B8A41D.quest_subtitle: "a QIO dashboard is used with the QIO drive array to display and access items that have been imported into the QIO system"
	quest.049BDED68524411F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6train observer&r will look at a specific part of the train track and detect when a train is crossing that specific section of track. It will give out a redstone signal when it detects a train going over that piece of track"
		""
		"The &6train observer&r can also only detect when a specific cargo is being held within the train."
	]
	quest.049BDED68524411F.quest_subtitle: "Watches for trains"
	quest.04D70707F44E6366.title: "Locate a &6Deep Dark&r"
	quest.05821667594CB9D1.quest_desc: ["&6Andesite casing&r is one of the most used items in the start of create it is used to make a bunch of helpful blocks to make progress"]
	quest.05821667594CB9D1.quest_subtitle: "Right click a stripped log with an &6andesite alloy&r"
	quest.05D344B86D2AD2AA.title: "Build a &dNether Portal&r"
	quest.05DE72DD68A60883.title: "Obtain any log"
	quest.05FEB18C9CA1B43A.quest_subtitle: "crushes ingots into dust for crafting"
	quest.062748AC02A28EE0.quest_subtitle: "increases the amount of energy a machine can hold and its efficiency"
	quest.06C15BD0F0FA38A1.quest_subtitle: "a better version of the solar generator"
	quest.06CD5DEE6AA5CAD2.quest_desc: ["The &61x1 drawer&r holds a total of &632 stacks&r of the dedicated item"]
	quest.06CD5DEE6AA5CAD2.quest_subtitle: "What it holds"
	quest.07E67470E2439059.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 3"
	quest.083D458032F0325C.quest_desc: ["The &bME Export Bus&f periodically spits items in its whitelist filter out to whatever external storage the bus is facing. Unlike the Import Bus, the Export Bus cannot work without being filtered."]
	quest.086AD7A1AFF55669.quest_subtitle: "the small connector can connect up to 4 wires"
	quest.09582A31B8474BD2.quest_subtitle: "increases machine speed"
	quest.0B218DD73FE8D985.quest_desc: [
		"If you did that last quest correctly, you should have turned that singularity into a pair of &bQuantum Entangled Singularities&f. These new singularities are used to link together a ring-shaped device known as a &eQuantum Network Bridge&f."
		""
		"When two of these individual rings have been linked using the Quantum Entangled Singularities and jumpstarted with some AE power (e.g. an energy cell), an ME network can be expanded wirelessly on the other side of the bridge, across either long distances or even dimensions."
	]
	quest.0B218DD73FE8D985.title: "Quantum Network Bridge"
	quest.0BA64F85C84913A8.quest_desc: ["This works if cheats are enabled. If you dont have them enabled, temorarily enable them before claiming this quest"]
	quest.0BEFC459747CC74A.quest_subtitle: "Start producing some Polonium with the Solar Neutron Activator!"
	quest.0BEFC459747CC74A.title: "Lets Start With Producing Polonium!"
	quest.0C2DA88F47809268.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 2"
	quest.0C5F842394B5832E.title: "Collect 3 &dWither Skulls&r and 4 soul sand"
	quest.0CAAA8CED77A9500.quest_subtitle: "smart reactors!"
	quest.0DF647AEBF066120.quest_subtitle: "what are you compensating for"
	quest.0DF88AEA8B5BE8BE.quest_subtitle: "this wire spool can connect to high current connectors"
	quest.0E1B8E7D4767B33F.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 1 Plus"
	quest.0EE6AA9F0D4C8FAE.quest_subtitle: "transports fluids and gases any and everywhere"
	quest.0F9323943E05DED3.quest_desc: [
		"The Fission Reactor is a high-yield energy system essential for late-game progression."
		""
		"Its primary use is for producing Polonium and Plutonium, vital for the final tier of technology."
	]
	quest.0F9323943E05DED3.quest_subtitle: "Nuclear Fission"
	quest.0F9323943E05DED3.title: "Build your first reactor!"
	quest.103D52C06B3BC840.quest_subtitle: "a highly efficient superfuel!"
	quest.118D443869E39F1A.quest_desc: ["The &6portable storage interface&r needs 2 to work correctly, one of them on the machine and the other one not attached to the machine and with a 1 block gap and aligned with eachother before the machine is started so that on each rotation is will deposit the excess items into the stationary one"]
	quest.118D443869E39F1A.quest_subtitle: "Move items from farms to storage"
	quest.11CBF2CE777F8CDF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blaze burners&r as used to heat up the basin which is needed to make certain things like &6brass&r"
		""
		"To collect blazes in a &6blaze burner&r you can either right click a blaze with an empty &6blaze burner&r or right click a blaze spawner to collect them"
	]
	quest.11CBF2CE777F8CDF.quest_subtitle: "Used to heat a basin below a mixer"
	quest.11CBF2CE777F8CDF.title: "Blaze Burner"
	quest.12439C71DDAC0E7C.quest_subtitle: "makes more from less"
	quest.12BE4EBECF60E611.quest_subtitle: "16x base storage capacity"
	quest.133696D3887F1B9D.title: "Enter &5The End&r"
	quest.1348995F64A94396.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCrafting Monitor&f displays the overall item being crafted, along with the remaining quantity of that item still being crafted."
		""
		"Both the base AE2 monitor and the MEGA monitor function identically, but are provided for aesthetic purposes."
	]
	quest.13E39EE147F3A618.quest_subtitle: "Make a sword"
	quest.13E39EE147F3A618.title: "Ready for combat"
	quest.140DE53DC0FCD9F4.quest_desc: [
		"The &bME Annihilation Plane&f can be used to automatically break any blocks in front of it and return anything dropped by the block directly to the ME network."
		""
		"As an added bonus, the Annihilation Plane can be enchanted in the same way as a regular digging tool, affecting block drops in the same way as that enchanted tool would. This makes it ideal for processing ore blocks when enchanted with Fortune, for example."
		""
		"Any added enchantments significantly increase the amount of energy used by the plane every time a block is broken. Enchanting the plane with &eEfficiency&f will decrease the overall energy use incurred by all other enchantments, while the &eUnbreaking&f enchantment gives the plane the chance to only use any energy sometimes, similarly to Unbreaking on regular tools."
	]
	quest.1419B4D48DDCF990.quest_subtitle: "can be made with (1 sugar, 1 cinderflour, and 2 biomass) can be used in blaze burners as a fuel source"
	quest.142036464D1B5F9E.quest_subtitle: "who needs backpacks when you have a portable QIO dashboard!"
	quest.153C2830E21BD9AE.title: "Shulkers FTW"
	quest.1556359BFFD07E29.quest_subtitle: "the rolling mill make rods and wires out of ingots and sheets using rotational energy"
	quest.15564C11744D6AA0.quest_desc: ["Once you have obtained a full set of the required &eInscriber Presses&r, it's time to start making some &eProcessors&f. These are an important crafting ingredient used to make the large majority of ME-connected devices."]
	quest.15564C11744D6AA0.quest_subtitle: "essential for AE's tools/machines"
	quest.15564C11744D6AA0.title: "Processors"
	quest.155AD7777C4276DD.quest_subtitle: "safety apparel"
	quest.156AA919AC78D534.quest_desc: [
		"&6Elevators&r are a really fun way to travel vertically."
		""
		"&6Mr Beardstone&r has done a video on how to make one, feel free to check it out"
	]
	quest.156AA919AC78D534.quest_subtitle: "Vertical travel"
	quest.16299B9AE87257DC.quest_desc: [
		"the &bWireless Terminal&f functions identically to a regular terminal, but wirelessly. Go figure."
		""
		"Before a wireless terminal can be used to access a network, it must first be &elinked&f to the network via the &eSecurity Terminal&f you made earlier. If it is not linked to a network, or is out of either range or power, the terminal will not function."
		""
		"Wireless terminals can also be upgraded with &eEnergy Cards&f to provide a larger internal battery."
	]
	quest.168894C6A9FB3E85.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 1"
	quest.1710B3D05215A71E.quest_desc: [
		"&bP2P&f (peer-to-peer) is a powerful system within AE2, allowing for the transfer of items, fluids and even more without the need for any intermediary ME storage."
		""
		"Right-clicking on a P2P tunnel with certain items will &eattune&f the tunnel into one capable of transferring something else, such as items through pipes, energy through cables, redstone signals and (by default) even ME connections themselves."
		""
		"P2P tunnels must be linked to one another with the use of a &eMemory Card&f, detailed in the next quest."
	]
	quest.1710B3D05215A71E.title: "P2P Tunnels"
	quest.17D3020E559009E3.quest_desc: [
		"When you place the &6water wheel&r you can flow water over it to start producing stress units, it will produce the same stress whether 1 or more sides are covered in water"
		""
		"You can change the aesthetic of the water wheel by right clicking it with a plank and it will appear like that plank type"
	]
	quest.17D3020E559009E3.quest_subtitle: "A method of stress generation"
	quest.17F29706CE9A846E.quest_desc: [
		"AE2 and Refined Storage are very similar in terms of storing items, except when it comes to AE2 having &eType Limits&r within the drives. Some people prefer not worring about item types or type limits."
		""
		"This is where &dAE2Things&f comes in. Alongside the two bonus machines, AE2Things predominantly features an alternative to the standard cell called the \"ME Deep Item Storage disK\", or the &bME DISK Drive&f for short."
		""
		"The DISK Drive, as one can imagine, functions very similarly to, if not the exact same as, the storage disks from &bRefined Storage&f. Primarily, they &odo not have type limits&r."
		""
		"Items stored in a DISK each count as a whole byte regardless of \"type\", meaning they can store significantly fewer items than equivalently-sized standard cells overall."
	]
	quest.17F29706CE9A846E.title: "&oDeep&r Item Storage"
	quest.18736449E1AADBCD.quest_desc: ["The &6brass casing&r is the upgrade of the &eandesite casing&r with it's ability to make better quality items for automation"]
	quest.18736449E1AADBCD.quest_subtitle: "The next generation of casing"
	quest.187518D514B536F4.quest_desc: ["The train controls are the block that is needed to allow your train to move once it's assembled. If you put 2 &6train controls&r in a single train then the train will be able to travel in both directions "]
	quest.187518D514B536F4.quest_subtitle: "Make a train move"
	quest.189E9A2E16E7C9F6.quest_subtitle: "used to make electrical devices"
	quest.18DFB25DC48D8BF7.quest_desc: [
		"The Spatial Containment Structure (SCS) consists of a cage of &bSpatial Pylons&f covering the volume you wish to enclose in a Spatial IO cell. At the absolute minimum, an SCS requires three lines of spatial pylon blocks, one for each dimension of the space being contained (length, width, height)."
		""
		"However, Spatial IO is an extremely power-hungry feature, especially when trying to capture much larger spaces (up to 128x128x128). Having more spatial pylons included in the SCS around the desired volume will increase its overall &eefficiency&f, allowing it to use less energy to capture."
		""
		"Also, be mindful that each individual pylon (regardless of its length) takes up one channel. For particularly large spaces, you may wish to build a dedicated network with a controller to fit all the required pylons."
	]
	quest.18DFB25DC48D8BF7.title: "Spatial Pylon"
	quest.18F32424F2F77626.title: "Chemical Infuser, For Uranium Hexafluoride!"
	quest.19847BB7C8D7EE79.quest_subtitle: "the main foundation of all machines!"
	quest.19847BB7C8D7EE79.title: "Steel Casing"
	quest.19FE6C712D83EF67.quest_subtitle: "wire can be made by putting sheets into the rolling mill"
	quest.19FE6C712D83EF67.title: "any wire"
	quest.1A913DF23D8F0B9D.quest_subtitle: "main component used in solar generators"
	quest.1AAF0B31B47AF23D.quest_desc: [
		"Individual ME devices can also be configured to respond to redstone signals. When upgraded with a &bRedstone Card&f, a device can be configured to do work only when powered with redstone or otherwise as needed."
		""
		"This behavour can also apply to entire &osections&r of an ME network by using an &bME Toggle Bus&f. This allows a section of the network on the other side of the bus to come online only when the bus is powered by redstone, or to go offline if using an &einverted&f toggle bus."
	]
	quest.1AAF0B31B47AF23D.title: "Redstone-Controlled ME"
	quest.1AB5695E3FFA5338.title: "Make a &dNetherite Ingot&r"
	quest.1ABAF66FF1313E57.quest_desc: ["The &6hose pulley&r has the ability to pull liquids from the world to be transported, if the source the pulley is pulling from is larger than 10,000 blocks then it classes it as an infinite source of liquid"]
	quest.1ABAF66FF1313E57.quest_subtitle: "Moving Liquid"
	quest.1AC0EC7056C0DCD4.quest_subtitle: "Craft any drawer"
	quest.1AC0EC7056C0DCD4.title: "Drawers"
	quest.1AE0D9AA55977585.quest_subtitle: "300% ore processing"
	quest.1AF4019667A352B1.quest_desc: ["The &6trim&r is a really handy utility block within the mod. It is used to link up drawers to eachother when they don't directly touch, it's pretty much a fake drawer as it cannot store any items within it but is still part of your total drawer network"]
	quest.1AF4019667A352B1.quest_subtitle: "Connect drawer without worrying of loosing items into them"
	quest.1AFE8D1CE55C1527.title: "Enter a &dBastion&r"
	quest.1B686954D34A0F23.quest_desc: [
		"The &bQuartz Wrench&f does what any regular tech mod wrench would do. It rotates blocks and devices along the face you right-click on and dismantles them when right-clicked while sneaking."
		""
		"AE2's wrench comes in both certus and nether quartz flavours."
	]
	quest.1B686954D34A0F23.quest_subtitle: "Does exactly what you'd expect."
	quest.1B686954D34A0F23.title: "Wrench"
	quest.1BFE0FCD48DD1C61.quest_desc: ["The &6item drain&r has the ability to take liquid out of a container and then it stores it until it it is piped out into a container"]
	quest.1BFE0FCD48DD1C61.quest_subtitle: "Fluid extraction"
	quest.1E09D69C2EC5DC5F.quest_subtitle: "increases a gas machines efficency"
	quest.1E49278F910726F5.quest_subtitle: "makes noisy machines quieter"
	quest.1E5F309B85AA57AC.quest_subtitle: "makes specific machines force load chunks"
	quest.1F7DFA5AA65F2812.quest_desc: [
		"The &bAcceleration Card&f, depending on the device being upgraded with it, will either increase the speed at which the device operates or allow the device to carry out more operations in one go."
		""
		"In the case of the &eMolecular Assembler&f, a full set of 5 cards reduces the time taken for the MA to fulfil a craft from one second (with no cards) to one &otick&r."
	]
	quest.1FD08BC5DB50656F.quest_subtitle: "wood processing"
	quest.1FE273AE15FB9F43.quest_subtitle: "Gives a redstone signal base on the least full slot"
	quest.203A4C8942368590.quest_subtitle: "turns a &belite&r factory in a &dultimate&r factory"
	quest.2077D64428E9C067.quest_desc: [
		"An important concept within AE2 is a technique known as \"&esubnetting&f\", wherein an extra separate ME network (a &esubnetwork&f) acts in conjuction with the main network to perform some specialised function or process."
		""
		"What separates a subnetwork from a completely detached separate network is usually the use of the &bQuartz Fiber&f as a cable part. When placed between two otherwise unconnected lengths of cable, the Quartz Fiber transfers no data or channels between the two whatsoever, instead only transmitting power."
		""
		"Thus, a subnetwork on the other side of the Fiber can be powered wholly by the main network's power source, without requiring any extra dedicated powergen."
	]
	quest.20C0B4B05C8F4FC0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6mechanical crafter&r can be made into a multi block to craft different items, the biggest item it will need to craft is the crushing wheels"
		""
		"The largest size and shape of the crushing wheel is shown below with an X the O don't have any &6mechanical crafters&r"
		""
		"&6OXXXO&r"
		"&6XXXXX&r"
		"&6XXXXX&r"
		"&6XXXXX&r"
		"&6OXXXO&r"
	]
	quest.20C0B4B05C8F4FC0.quest_subtitle: "A large crafting table"
	quest.2182BBA062146DAA.quest_subtitle: "rods can be made by putting an ingot into the rolling mill"
	quest.2182BBA062146DAA.title: "any rod"
	quest.219932CB19258C16.quest_desc: ["The third tier of storage component, providing &e16384&f bytes of storage."]
	quest.219932CB19258C16.title: "16k Storage Component"
	quest.226171470A06E7E8.quest_subtitle: "Get 4 planks"
	quest.226171470A06E7E8.title: "Craft some planks"
	quest.22C4318523A43B49.quest_desc: [
		"&eTerminals&f provide access to any of the contents of an ME network. The standard &eME Terminal&f simply lists everything in the network as one large grid to pull from and insert into, akin to a single inventory."
		""
		"The &eME Crafting Terminal&f is an extension of the ME Terminal which also provides a built-in crafting grid, allowing for convenient crafting using any item contained in the network and visible through the terminal screen."
	]
	quest.22C4318523A43B49.title: "Terminals"
	quest.22D395ACA8E7B09C.title: "Chemical Oxidizer, for Sulfur Dioxide!"
	quest.234DC1702333EB18.quest_desc: ["The &dAEInfinityBooster&f add-on provides two bespoke wireless boosters allowing for infinite connectivity range, with optional cross-dimensional support."]
	quest.234DC1702333EB18.title: "AEInfinityBooster"
	quest.252245F4C408B9C9.quest_desc: ["&6Brass&r is the start of the next generation of create, it allows for crafting many more advanced options"]
	quest.252245F4C408B9C9.quest_subtitle: "The next era starts"
	quest.252245F4C408B9C9.title: "&6Brass ingots&r"
	quest.2575193E2B12DED1.quest_subtitle: "8x base storage capacity"
	quest.26E96DB0FA326797.quest_subtitle: "advanced sorting"
	quest.276C7899C807BED9.quest_subtitle: "the heat generator uses any burnable item to produce energy. (you can also surround it in lava to passively produce energy) "
	quest.2771124207DF211A.quest_desc: ["To make andesite alloy you will need &l&62 andesite&r&r and &l&62 iron or zinc nuggets&r&r"]
	quest.2771124207DF211A.quest_subtitle: "Make andesite alloy"
	quest.2771124207DF211A.title: "Make andesite alloy"
	quest.2793B9D07572E28A.quest_subtitle: "the electric motor uses energy to spin shafts and cogs"
	quest.27B28A53F0EFE604.title: "Enter &dThe Nether&r"
	quest.2893F483C10293E6.quest_desc: [
		"&lWelcome to &bApplied Energistics 2&f!"
		""
		"Applied Energistics 2 (or &oAE2&r for short) is an incredibly versatile &bdigital storage&f mod, allowing for extremely efficient storage and all sorts of automation capabilities to greatly augment your modded Minecraft experience from as early as you want to the very endgame."
		""
		"To get started with AE2, you will need to mine an important resource for the mod known as &bCertus Quartz&f. Its ore most frequently drops Certus Quartz &eDust&f, but you may be able to find a &eCrystal&f from it every once in a while."
	]
	quest.2893F483C10293E6.quest_subtitle: "Virtual Storage System"
	quest.2893F483C10293E6.title: "Applied Energistics 2"
	quest.2897FA291E5A38D8.quest_desc: ["The &bSpatial Anchor&f is a companion device from the Spatial IO lineage that simply functions as a chunk loader. When connected to an ME network, the Anchor will force-load all the chunks occupied by the ME network across all cables and devices, excluding subnetworks, as long as the network remains powered."]
	quest.29737F0807DB786E.quest_subtitle: "The base of all backpack upgrades"
	quest.29CAA4C5FF9CE492.quest_desc: ["The &6redstone contact&r is used to dictate where the elevator will stop at when the 2 contacts connect to eachother"]
	quest.29CAA4C5FF9CE492.quest_subtitle: "Part of the elevator"
	quest.2A56867DD6B2BA7B.quest_subtitle: "this wire spool can connect to high current connectors"
	quest.2A76D4477D487021.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2A76D4477D487021.quest_subtitle: "freeeeee fallin' without damage"
	quest.2A913D19CDBFCA66.quest_subtitle: "The key to lock and unlock drawers"
	quest.2A9C865610F8FD71.quest_subtitle: "basic storage"
	quest.2AA96619167BF9F9.quest_subtitle: "256x base storage capacity"
	quest.2AE513D9DCAF3402.quest_subtitle: "turns a &cadvanced&r factory into a &belite&r factory"
	quest.2B2552D2540B0A13.quest_desc: [
		"An efficient way to transport items"
		""
		"You can also use the &6belts&r to tranfer rotation force by connecting them to 2 &6shafts&r at either end of where you want to belt to go along"
		""
		"They do go diagonal but not always at some angles you can tell if it will as there will be rainbow particles showing it can be placed"
	]
	quest.2B2552D2540B0A13.quest_subtitle: "Crafted with 6 dried kelp"
	quest.2B26D7418173C28A.quest_desc: [
		"to get started with mekanism you will need to make a \"&6heat generator&r\" which produces energy from any burnable resource or when submerged in lava (you can alternatively use redstone dust to power machines), "
		""
		"and a \"&8metallurgic infuser&r\" which makes circuits and alloy for the start of mekanism."
		""
		"you can make 3 types of alloy in the metallurgic infuser. "
		"(&cinfused&r, &breinforced&r, and &5atomic&r)."
		""
		"you can also make a (&abasic control circuit&r)"
		"which has 4 tiers."
		"(&abasic&r, &cadvanced&r, &belite&r, and &5ultimate&r) "
	]
	quest.2B26D7418173C28A.quest_subtitle: "materials needed to get started with mekanism"
	quest.2B26D7418173C28A.title: "getting started"
	quest.2B31E6C1707D8195.quest_desc: ["The next thing to make to allow for wireless network access is the &bME Wireless Access Point&f. The Access Point is used to open the network to wireless access via a &ewireless terminal&f, and has a set (finite) range depending on how many &bWireless Boosters&f are inserted into the access point."]
	quest.2B4A47D50D527385.quest_subtitle: "No more Manual Mining!"
	quest.2BF65941798A7C5D.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2BF65941798A7C5D.quest_subtitle: "An advanced device for storing and providing energy"
	quest.2BF65941798A7C5D.title: "Energy Cube"
	quest.2C04B3BA507D5673.quest_desc: [
		"&bPatterns&f are what hold an encoded recipe to be fulfilled by a Pattern Provider. To encode a recipe onto a Pattern, the &bME Pattern Encoding Terminal&f must be used."
		""
		"Patterns can be set to hold either a regular &ecrafting&f recipe, which will require the use of a &eMolecular Assembler&f on the face of its Provider, or a more general \"&eprocessing&f\" recipe, wherein any input items can be sent out by the provider into some other machine block or specialised processing plant."
	]
	quest.2C04B3BA507D5673.title: "Patterns"
	quest.2DCF9C41FA7D28E4.quest_desc: ["The &6train station&r is the part that makes trains work. You can create a train from within gui of the train station. It's other job is as the place where the train will stop along a route, these are the place you enter into the &etrain schedule&r as the stopping locations"]
	quest.2DCF9C41FA7D28E4.quest_subtitle: "Waypoints for trains"
	quest.2E04B195B9812022.quest_subtitle: "turns a regular machine into a &abasic&r factory"
	quest.2E232FE3E08A0E7F.quest_desc: ["You can place &6large cogwheels&r at 90 degrees to eachother and it will change the direction of rotation"]
	quest.2E232FE3E08A0E7F.quest_subtitle: "The larger of the cogwheels"
	quest.2E5C4026EB6FEE60.quest_desc: ["This works if cheats are enabled. If you dont have them enabled, temorarily enable them before claiming this quest"]
	quest.2F16B6A173525277.quest_desc: [
		"The last piece of the puzzle for any large ME network is the &bME Controller&f."
		""
		"A controller supplies an ME Network with a far larger number of channels than the standard 8 channels for ad-hoc networks, providing 32 channels out of each face of the block for a total of 216 channels."
		""
		"That's only for a single-block controller, however, since the ME Controller is in fact a multi-block structure. The controller can be up to 7x7x7 blocks in size and can come in any freeform arrangement within that maximum size. Each individual block can then provide its own separate set of channels, so long as no single controller block is surrounded by 4 other blocks along the same plane."
		""
		"An ME Network may only contain one multiblock controller at any given time. Attempting to connect more than one controller on separate parts of the network will cause a conflict, shutting down the whole network."
	]
	quest.2F16B6A173525277.quest_subtitle: "almost a super computer"
	quest.2F556E7919582D2D.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCell Workbench&f allows for cells to be \"partitioned\" to hold specific items, i.e. given a whitelist filter. It also allows the cell to be upgraded with certain upgrade cards such as the Inverter Card, which sets the aforementioned whitelist to be a blacklist instead."
		""
		"Cells can also be given a higher or lower \"priority\" via the workbench, i.e. allow the cell to be the first to receive certain items until full, or made to wait for other higher-priority cells to fill up first."
	]
	quest.2FAFA92C1305602F.title: "basic energy storage upgrade II"
	quest.2FB231069D2E4E77.quest_desc: [
		"Each individual cell has a certain capacity dictated by the &ecomponent&f that the cell has been crafted with."
		""
		"The first of the components is the &b1k ME Storage Component&f, providing &e1024&f \"bytes\" of storage for a given cell. More on that later."
		""
		"Create the 1k Component, which will be combined with housing in the next quest."
	]
	quest.2FB231069D2E4E77.title: "Creating your first Storage Cell"
	quest.30E853CE699E669B.quest_desc: [
		"Before you can carry out an auto-crafting job, you need a device to actually store the request itself along with any interim items for multi-step crafts. This device is known as a &ecrafting CPU&f."
		""
		"A crafting CPU is a multiblock structure requiring at least one &bCrafting Storage&f block, optionally along with any other Crafting Unit. The multiblock can be made in any size, but must be a solid cuboid in order to form and function accordingly."
	]
	quest.3195A7AA874163CD.quest_desc: [
		"The &bEqual Distribution Card&f is an upgrade for storage cells that pre-allocates a certain amount of items that can be taken up by any individual type."
		""
		"This behaviour is comparable to something like a Functional Storage drawer, wherein each compartment holds a set number of stacks as opposed to allowing items from one compartment to leak into the others and crowd other kinds of items out."
	]
	quest.33ADE41526C39AFD.quest_desc: ["The &bOverflow Destruction Card&f is a cell upgrade that allows storage cells to delete (void) any items of a type already contained within them, when try to move into the cell and the cell is already full."]
	quest.34C409E6FF596E2A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6train schedule&r is helpful as you can decide what order a train goes from station to station and how long it is at the station before it departs for the next station."
		""
		"You can right click a mob on a &ered seat&r that is next to the train controls to set that mob as the train conductor and they will follow the train schedule"
	]
	quest.34C409E6FF596E2A.quest_subtitle: "Decide when trains move"
	quest.34CF8CC6400ACAB7.quest_desc: ["When you place a &9windmill bearing&r down you can place a plank on top of it to be able to connect the &bsails&r to"]
	quest.34CF8CC6400ACAB7.quest_subtitle: "An alternative stress source to water"
	quest.34CF8CC6400ACAB7.title: "Windmill Bearing"
	quest.352BABD3D2135968.quest_subtitle: "ZAP!"
	quest.3539259CBCC42BFB.title: "Chemical Infuser, for Sulfur Trioxide!"
	quest.3612EB73B9709015.quest_desc: ["The &6precision mechanism&r is used in making some more advanced items like the &6rotational speed controller&r and it requires a gold sheet to have 3 items deployed onto it in a specific order of small cogwheel then large cogwheel and lastely an iron nugget. That process is repeated 5x and has an 80% chance to work at the end"]
	quest.3612EB73B9709015.quest_subtitle: "Used in some crafting recipes"
	quest.361CCBD353D6FF34.quest_desc: [
		"With the 1k Storage Component, you can now craft yourself a 1k ME Item Storage Cell to start your digital item storage system. You'll most likely want the majority of your storage to be for items, so you'll probably want to make a few &bME Item Storage Cells&f."
		""
		"ME Item Storage Cells can each hold up to 63 different types of items. Each new type of item added to a cell will take up a certain fraction of the storage cell's total capacity in bytes. For each type already present, 1 \"byte\" counts for 8 items of that same type."
		""
		"As an example, a 1k Item Storage Cell containing only cobblestone can hold up to 8128 cobblestone (8*1024b - 8b/type * 1 type)."
		""
		"If a cell is empty, it can be repurposed by disassembling it into its respective component and housing. This is done by sneaking and right-clicking in the air with the cell in your hand."
	]
	quest.361CCBD353D6FF34.title: "Item Storage"
	quest.3681B7A0297F7028.quest_subtitle: "woop! woop! woop! "
	quest.3686BAC07C9F5E22.title: "Make a crafting table"
	quest.371A382CF1DDF2B2.quest_desc: ["The &bCapacity Card&f allows a bus upgraded with it to carry a larger filter. Import and Export buses upgraded with capacity cards can go from supporting only one filtered item each to their maximum nine-slot filter, while Storage buses will go from 18 slots to a maximum of 63."]
	quest.3814F467955D977B.quest_subtitle: "safety apparel"
	quest.384B9424DE8F6878.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 2"
	quest.387419E932117904.quest_desc: ["This works if cheats are enabled. If you dont have them enabled, temorarily enable them before claiming this quest"]
	quest.387419E932117904.title: "Turn off AE2 Channels"
	quest.38DE99A1019F4677.quest_desc: [
		"The induction matrix's capacity is defined by the number of Induction Cells and Providers you add."
		""
		"This reservoir will absorb the output from high-yield generators and provide large amounts of power to high-tier machinery."
	]
	quest.38DE99A1019F4677.quest_subtitle: "a highly conductive energy capacitor for massive energy storage"
	quest.38DE99A1019F4677.title: "High-Density Energy Reservoir"
	quest.397165BB305A887E.quest_desc: [
		"These cells can hold most chemicals from Mekanism, including gases, pigments and ore slurries, but they will &o&lnot&r hold anything radioactive such as nuclear waste."
		""
		"&dMEGA Cells&f also in turn integrates directly with Applied Mekanistics to provide higher tiers of chemical cells, though with the same radioactivity restriction as the standard cells."
	]
	quest.397165BB305A887E.title: "Chemical Storage"
	quest.39AD444F5F568CC9.quest_subtitle: "The key to show or hide quanity on drawers"
	quest.39E6CA577F59AB93.quest_subtitle: "Destroys items when the drawer gets full"
	quest.3A1FD20417D15F80.quest_desc: ["&6Super glue&r is the key part of all create multi blocks as it makes sure all the parts stay as one when the machine is started"]
	quest.3A1FD20417D15F80.quest_subtitle: "Getting stuck in"
	quest.3A1FD20417D15F80.title: "Super Glue"
	quest.3A27E71555DD0887.title: "Obtain an &6Elytra&r"
	quest.3A57232C88B44DD7.quest_desc: [
		""
		""
		"&dThere are no further quests to follow, And the whole world is open for your expansion."
		""
		"&r"
		""
		"&dThanks for playing!"
		""
		"&r"
		""
