		"You beat &l&6Create&r &9Energistics&r&r"
		""
		"&r"
		""
		"&d– Nova and the Team&r"
	]
	quest.3A57232C88B44DD7.quest_subtitle: "&6 Mastery Reached"
	quest.3A57232C88B44DD7.title: "&zMODPACK COMPLETE&r"
	quest.3ACBE9B17453B4B5.quest_subtitle: "Sleep at night without setting spawn"
	quest.3ACBE9B17453B4B5.title: "Craft a sleeping bag"
	quest.3B3660B502B5E741.quest_subtitle: "uses the wind to produce energy"
	quest.3B42CCC19D23EC6D.quest_desc: ["The second tier of storage component, providing &e4096&f bytes of storage."]
	quest.3B42CCC19D23EC6D.title: "4k Storage Component"
	quest.3B76AD708C591A48.quest_desc: [
		"The &6mechanical press&r is used for a lot of different things, like making sheets or some recipes using a basin"
		""
		"The &6depot&r is used to hold items on one block"
	]
	quest.3B76AD708C591A48.quest_subtitle: "Helpful for making a lot of things"
	quest.3B76AD708C591A48.title: "Mechanical Press and Depot"
	quest.3BF442790F0F281C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6train signal&r helps with keeping trains from going the wrong way as a train won't pass over a &6train signal&r if it is facing the wrong direction."
		"The &6signal&r can be made a 2 way &6signal&r by having one on either side of the track, having a 2 way &6signal&r will make it so a train can pass it if the scheduled station is on the other side"
	]
	quest.3BF442790F0F281C.quest_subtitle: "Help's with train flow"
	quest.3DDB0DDA7571B2C1.quest_desc: [
		"The &bME Level Emitter&f, when configured with a specific item and quantity of it to respond to, will emit a redstone signal depending on whether that item stored in the network either falls below, goes above or equals the given quantity."
		""
		"This can be used, for example, to automatically switch certain machines on with redstone to auto-craft a resource when it falls below a given minimum amount."
	]
	quest.3E0E5CFDA096D590.quest_subtitle: "this spool can connect to low current connectors and provides pretty lighting"
	quest.3E10D349E202CC89.quest_subtitle: "Aesthetic trapdoor"
	quest.3E3DF8E967D95DB0.quest_desc: [
		"When using a 64k storage component or higher, the Matter Condenser becomes able to condense significantly more to produce a &bSingularity&f. A single singularity requires 256000 items to be voided. That's exactly &o4000 stacks&r!"
		""
		"See what happens when you throw this singularity on the ground with a piece of &eender dust&f. You'll have to deal some damage to the surroundings while you're at it, but thankfully AE2 offers its own &bTiny TNT&f to minimise that."
	]
	quest.3E3DF8E967D95DB0.title: "Hyper-Condensed Matter"
	quest.3E666752E4B40376.quest_desc: [
		"The &6contraption control&r is used as the interface of the elevator for the player to look at and scroll up or "
		"down on the mouse to select the level"
	]
	quest.3E666752E4B40376.quest_subtitle: "Part of the elevator"
	quest.3ED77CA15F93C152.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Wrench&r is used to pick up create items really easily, just shift right click a create block to pick it up"
		""
		"It can also rotate blocks by just regular right clicking on a side"
	]
	quest.3ED77CA15F93C152.quest_subtitle: "The most used item in create"
	quest.3F28400EE8FFE9A9.quest_subtitle: "Collect nether wart and soul sand"
	quest.3F7F6896CB7F5120.quest_subtitle: "holds any fluid"
	quest.3F85C2E198ACEE74.title: "Upgrading your pickaxe"
	quest.3FBF24E53B57CBF0.quest_desc: ["The Fission Reactor requires continuous steam output and water return to prevent overheating and catastrophic failure."]
	quest.3FBF24E53B57CBF0.quest_subtitle: "Thermal Cooling"
	quest.3FBF24E53B57CBF0.title: "build your first turbine!"
	quest.403826F48A2AC639.quest_subtitle: "the straw is made with 1 bamboo in the rolling mill. the straw can be used on a blaze burner allowing it to intake liquid fuel"
	quest.41D89CBE62DE47F6.quest_subtitle: "the accumulator uses connectors to store and transfer energy"
	quest.424A76544E1F0BA5.quest_subtitle: "can be used on a train or contraption to acces stored energy within them"
	quest.4293CA293BD1C56F.quest_subtitle: "400% ore processing"
	quest.42959B6F1D614D70.quest_desc: ["You can place &6small cogwheels&r next to eachother to keep roational force sideways but the rotations will change from cogwheel to cogwheel"]
	quest.42959B6F1D614D70.quest_subtitle: "The smaller of the cogwheels"
	quest.42B7BE55C9EE3CFF.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome! You’re stepping into a completely overhauled world packed with high-tier technology and endless opportunities to explore."
		""
		""
		"This questbook is your primary guide—providing a clear path to help you kickstart your survival!"
		""
		"&l"
		""
		"&dHav"
		""
		"&r"
		""
		"(a modpack created by &bnova&r)"
		"contributors: &9JakeDestroyer&r &4TheBunnyOrikami&r"
	]
	quest.42B7BE55C9EE3CFF.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to &6Create &9Energistics"
	quest.42B7BE55C9EE3CFF.title: "&lIntroduction to &6Create &9Energistics"
	quest.432111807A61E6C6.quest_subtitle: "Keep track of what you want to do"
	quest.43496DF129AA9132.quest_subtitle: "The start of upgrading your storage capabilities"
	quest.442159787F607B8E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6crushing wheel&r is used to start processing raw resources more automatically"
		""
		"Some natural spawning blocks from create can be crushed to get resources the list is:"
		""
		"&cCrimsite&r is crushed to get a 40% chance at raw crushed Iron and a nugget"
		"&bAsurine&r is crushed to get a 30% chance at raw crushed Zinc and a nugget"
		"&aVeridium&r is crushed to get a 80% chance at raw crushed Copper and a nugget"
		"&eOchrum&r is crushed to get a 20% chance at raw crushed Gold and a nugget"
	]
	quest.442159787F607B8E.quest_subtitle: "Crushing stuff"
	quest.443868FD42BD73C8.quest_desc: ["The &6mechanical speed controller&r is a easier way to speed up rotational speeds, you can right click it and set the speed you want it to spin at"]
	quest.443868FD42BD73C8.quest_subtitle: "Replaces the cog wheel method"
	quest.4484A99C98B1D119.quest_desc: ["All upgrades from Sophisticated Backpacks can be turned into Storage upgrades"]
	quest.4484A99C98B1D119.quest_subtitle: "The base of all storage upgrades!"
	quest.457F1F059FD8B0CE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6train door&r has 3 modes and each of the modes decide how the door will intereact."
		""
		"The normal mode lets the player interact with the door but it also will auto open and shut depending on whether the machine is moving or not"
		""
		"The manual mode lets the player interact with the door like it's a regular door"
		""
		"The special mode doesn't let the player interact and will only open and close when moving or with a redstone signal (shift + right click will override the special mode)"
	]
	quest.457F1F059FD8B0CE.quest_subtitle: "Fancy door"
	quest.4597D3B3BDC2BED5.quest_desc: [
		"The &bMolecular Assembler&f is AE2's equivalent of an automatic crafting table, required to fulfil any and all &ecrafting&f pattern jobs."
		""
		"Molecular Assemblers are capable of transferring power and channels to other ME devices connected to it, but will not themselves take up a channel. Up to 6 MAs can be connected to a single Pattern Provider (if employed) to allow for more crafts to be done in parallel."
		""
		"MAs also each have their own dedicated slot for a single crafting pattern, allowing them to function standalone when powered. When operated in this way, any matching items inserted into the MA will be automatically crafted into the result of the pattern."
	]
	quest.45EC7DB841938E4D.quest_subtitle: "safety apparel"
	quest.46018883B4C50E4B.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.46018883B4C50E4B.quest_subtitle: "uses any burnable gas to produce energy (e.g. hydrogen, ethylene)"
	quest.47008815B9B9A0F8.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 4"
	quest.47543DD3473D06CC.title: "basic energy storage upgrade III"
	quest.47A34C2267D6EB1E.quest_desc: ["The &6harvester&r will automatically harvest crops when added to a machine"]
	quest.47A34C2267D6EB1E.quest_subtitle: "Crop harvesting"
	quest.47DAAA307A2F53A2.quest_desc: ["This device provides information of ambient radiation"]
	quest.47DAAA307A2F53A2.title: "Geiger Counter"
	quest.48551FD85AD3B1FF.quest_subtitle: "fluid movement"
	quest.48573F9B8B326804.title: "Summon and kill &dThe Wither&r"
	quest.4947B8C2A368E9FF.quest_subtitle: "the spool can be crafted into a wire filled spool with enough wires"
	quest.49B578E166B0F6AF.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.49B578E166B0F6AF.quest_subtitle: "You have successfully synthesized fissile fuel!"
	quest.49B578E166B0F6AF.title: "Isotopic Centrifuge, for Fissile Fuel!"
	quest.4A3BBB249A91808F.quest_desc: [
		"The Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer allows item &dtransmutation&r"
		"(e.g. coal to diamonds)."
	]
	quest.4A3BBB249A91808F.quest_subtitle: "&dTransmutation&r"
	quest.4A5BF2FB43FDC920.quest_subtitle: "chemical/gas movement"
	quest.4A8C5E90A276FDA7.quest_subtitle: "holds any chemical/gas"
	quest.4A9D0D014C61CB7B.quest_desc: ["The &6sturdy sheets&r mark the start of the train age, you will benefit from having lava and obsidian generating passively at this point if you plan to have an expansive and grand rail line throughout your world"]
	quest.4A9D0D014C61CB7B.quest_subtitle: "The start of the great railways"
	quest.4B3D35E2B7562509.quest_subtitle: "2x base storage capacity"
	quest.4B4B3352870D70EC.title: "Collect chorus fruit and flower"
	quest.4BF0BB763BFFACF0.quest_desc: [
		"Arguably the most important resource you will need next is &eFluix&f, used throughout the vast majority of AE2 devices and serving as a base for crafting all of the cabling within an ME network."
		""
		"As a head start, any meteorite you find in the world will contain a core of 6 Fluix Blocks, for a total of 24 crystals per meteorite."
		""
		"However, you'll typically want to mass produce these, and the way to do so is to start with making &bFluix Dust&f by throwing &eNether Quartz&f, &e&oCharged&r&e Certus quartz&r and &eRedstone&f together in a pool of water. Then you can grow the dust into crystals in the same way as you would with Certus Quartz via seeds."
	]
	quest.4BF0BB763BFFACF0.title: "Fluix Crystal"
	quest.4C076BCACF6E16CA.title: "Defeat the &5Ender Dragon&r"
	quest.4CCDD0283D36BD8A.quest_desc: ["The &6train casing&r is the main block use to create all things train related"]
	quest.4CCDD0283D36BD8A.quest_subtitle: "Almost ready to assemble"
	quest.4CFB72C84BA53782.quest_desc: ["The &6millstone&r has the ability to crush many items"]
	quest.4CFB72C84BA53782.quest_subtitle: "Can make dye and other things"
	quest.4CFB72C84BA53782.title: "Millstone"
	quest.4D60B83A920D5165.quest_desc: ["the configurator allows you to configure the inputs and outputs on machines and wires"]
	quest.4D60B83A920D5165.quest_subtitle: "Let The Production Begin!"
	quest.4D60B83A920D5165.title: "Configurator"
	quest.4D84C35EF223370E.quest_subtitle: "  a QIO system is used for storing items of different types. using a QIO exporter and importer you can move items across long distances and dimensions"
	quest.4D84C35EF223370E.title: "make your first QIO system"
	quest.4DC3AC792B3B91E2.quest_desc: ["The &6mechanical bearing&r is the centre piece of machines, it lets you build any machine onto it and becomes the central spinning part of the machine"]
	quest.4DC3AC792B3B91E2.quest_subtitle: "The key to machines"
	quest.4DC3AC792B3B91E2.title: "Mechanical Bearing"
	quest.4DE18CB6F344809A.title: "Make a fully powered beacon"
	quest.4E8A05C3BFA80540.quest_desc: [
		"Arguably the most important aspect of Applied Energistics 2 is its storage system, making use of digital &eStorage Cells&f. These cells are accessible through either an &eME Chest&r for single cells, or an &eME Drive&r for multiple cells."
		""
		"The &bME Chest&f holds a single Cell at a time, which can then be read from and written to from any other terminal on the same network. The ME Chest itself also provides its own terminal screen on the top with specific access only to the cell it contains."
		""
		"The &bME Drive&f can hold up to 10 assorted Storage Cells in the space of a single block and a single ME channel. However, it does not provide its own terminal screen, requiring some external terminal elsewhere on the network for storage access."
	]
	quest.4E8A05C3BFA80540.quest_subtitle: "file system for items"
	quest.4E8A05C3BFA80540.title: "The Storage"
	quest.4F4415CE4EC30024.quest_desc: ["The &6fluid tank&r is a easy way to store a large amount of liquid. The biggest it can be is a 3x3 base and upto 30 tall, which stores a crazy amount"]
	quest.4F4415CE4EC30024.quest_subtitle: "A large liquid container"
	quest.4F616AAC367E79A4.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4F616AAC367E79A4.quest_subtitle: "You have successfully synthesized Polonium"
	quest.4F616AAC367E79A4.title: "Polonium"
	quest.4FFE92F9BD1FA9F9.quest_desc: ["The &62x2 drawer&r holds &68 stacks&r in each of the option slots"]
	quest.4FFE92F9BD1FA9F9.quest_subtitle: "What it holds"
	quest.4FFF45F1A84216ED.quest_subtitle: "what are you compensating for"
	quest.5062F049AFCBC5CB.quest_desc: ["You will polish the &drose quartz&r to use in making electron tubes"]
	quest.5062F049AFCBC5CB.quest_subtitle: "Off hand the sand paper and then right click with the &drose quartz&r"
	quest.5062F049AFCBC5CB.title: "&dPolished Rose Quartz&r"
	quest.51236544BFEF487B.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have your first Charged Certus Quartz Crystal, it's time to put it to use on the final important step towards getting up and running with AE2."
		""
		"The &bMeteorite Compass&f will point towards the nearest chunk it can find containing &bSky Stone&f, which generate naturally as part of large &eMeteorites&f. These can be either on the surface or underground"
	]
	quest.51236544BFEF487B.quest_subtitle: "required materials"
	quest.51236544BFEF487B.title: "Inscriber Presses"
	quest.51DE3157DE3E57B8.quest_desc: [
		"Storage is nice and all that, but what good is a storage system if it's clogged up with raw materials needing to be crafted and processed into something and you're still stuck with having to do so manually?"
		""
		"AE2's &eauto-crafting&f system begins with the &bME Pattern Provider&f. The Pattern Provider holds certain items called &bPatterns&f (covered in the next quest) which are programmed to hold some recipe that turns input items into a certain output. Up to 9 patterns can fit in one provider."
		""
		"You'll often be making use of multiple pattern providers scattered all throughout your base, which is why it's useful to have a &bPattern Access Terminal&f to remotely access the contents of any and all providers on your wider ME network."
	]
	quest.51DE3157DE3E57B8.title: "Auto-Crafting"
	quest.5233A447BAA4593C.quest_desc: ["The &bME Smart Cable&f and &bDense Smart Cable&f function identically to the covered cables in terms of channel distribution, but will also visibly display the amount of channels they are using as coloured lines along themselves."]
	quest.5233A447BAA4593C.title: "Advanced Cabling"
	quest.523853C1C4E688BA.quest_desc: ["The fourth tier of storage component, providing &e65536&f bytes of storage."]
	quest.523853C1C4E688BA.title: "64k Storage Component"
	quest.524F570AFCE37194.quest_desc: [
		"This very expensive technology converts plasma into a huge amount of energy."
		""
		"Fusion requires deuterium and tritium generated by \"filtered pumps\" and \"solar neutron activators\"."
	]
	quest.524F570AFCE37194.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Energy Production"
	quest.524F570AFCE37194.title: "   build your first fusion reactor!"
	quest.525F25F4ADE45B50.quest_desc: [
		"The &bME Formation Plane&f acts similarly to the Storage Bus, but treats the world itself as its storage medium. In other words, it will place down any block in its filter directly in front of itself."
		""
		"This can be useful for situations where a block can be processed simply by placing it and breaking it with a certain tool."
	]
	quest.52B7ED1D537434BA.title: "Chemical Infuser, for Sulfuric Acid!"
	quest.5389403FB37C765F.quest_subtitle: "hydrogen powered flight"
	quest.54C243CD0E3D8F80.quest_desc: ["&6Andesite funnels&r are used to pull items out of a chest one at a time, they will drop the items onto a &6belt&r or &6depot&r below it"]
	quest.54C243CD0E3D8F80.quest_subtitle: "Crafted with andesite alloy and dried kelp"
	quest.54C243CD0E3D8F80.title: "Andesite Funnel"
	quest.55186B8602689B66.quest_desc: [
		"The &bMemory Card&f is a tool with to different functions. The simplest of the two is to save various devices' configurations (such as whitelist filters) to be copied over to another device of the same kind."
		""
		"The second function of a memory card is to link &eP2P tunnels&f together. When doing so, the P2P tunnel being linked will be assigned a unique ID, which is stored on the memory card for further linking."
	]
	quest.5720A87944651114.quest_subtitle: "The labels glow in the dark"
	quest.57BACA91541F39D0.quest_subtitle: "Gives a redstone signal based on how full the drawer is"
	quest.58EC279CEC40AB2D.quest_subtitle: "turns a &abasic&r factory into a &cadvanced&r factory"
	quest.5905FC5707210B9D.quest_subtitle: "seed oil can be made with any type of seed in a compactor"
	quest.5983B2257D9E8EE8.quest_desc: ["This works if cheats are enabled. If you dont have them enabled, temorarily enable them before claiming this quest"]
	quest.59AEBA331EE4F644.quest_desc: ["The &6steam engine&r is a way to produce stress units using heat and water. When placing a &6steam engine&r on the side of a &efluid tank&r that's full of water and has a heat source below it it will start to create rotational force. The higher the heat source the faster the &6steam engine&r will move. The best source for the highest output is &eblaze burners&r being fed blaze cakes to super heat the water tank. At the highest level you can add 8 &6steam engines&r to the tank."]
	quest.59AEBA331EE4F644.quest_subtitle: "A different stress unit source"
	quest.59C8CFE7F44925C0.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.59C8CFE7F44925C0.quest_subtitle: "This barrel is designed to safely contain nuclear waste"
	quest.59C8CFE7F44925C0.title: "Waste Barrel"
	quest.5A7B1CB5FB1E7D0C.quest_subtitle: "Make a shovel"
	quest.5A7B1CB5FB1E7D0C.title: "The dirt destroyer"
	quest.5A9AD38730B9D76C.quest_subtitle: "the alternator uses rotational energy to make power. the faster it spins the more power that is made"
	quest.5AA3E5DFECB4AC4D.quest_desc: [
		"Naturally, AE2 provides its own way to dramatically speed up crystal growth, assuming you don't happen to have Mekanism's Enrichment Chamber on hand."
		""
		"Placing a water source block within a full set of 5 &bCrystal Growth Accelerators&f will reduce the growing time of certus crystals and seeds "
	]
	quest.5AFAFAF852763B40.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.5AFAFAF852763B40.quest_subtitle: "Use this, for the last step to make both plutonium and Polonium!"
	quest.5AFAFAF852763B40.title: "Fluid To Item!"
	quest.5BAEEB32E0418EE2.quest_subtitle: "cheap energy production"
	quest.5BB887411B8B38FA.quest_desc: [
		"As for wirelessly expanding the ME Network itself, the first step is admittedly somewhat unorthodox."
		""
		"The &bMatter Condenser&f is AE2's take on a trash can, voiding any items inserted into it. When fitted with a &eStorage Component&f, however, the condenser can harness some left-over energy from the item being voided and store it to make two special crafting items out of enough concentrated energy."
		""
		"The first of these two items is the &bMatter Ball&f, requiring at least a 1k storage component and 256 items' worth of voided material."
	]
	quest.5BB887411B8B38FA.title: "Condensed Matter"
	quest.5C22E3103544B120.quest_desc: [
		"To connect the vast majority of your ME network together, you will need some cable. &eME Glass Cable&f is the first and most basic kind of cable, and you'll be making this all throughout as the first step towards crafting the other kinds of cable."
		""
		"Both glass cables and their &ecovered&f counterpart can carry up to 8 channels along a single section of cabling. Unlike glass cables, covered cables can subsequently be crafted into &edense&f covered cables, capable of carrying up to 32 channels. However, most \"multipart\" devices such as buses and terminals cannot be directly attached to dense cables, requiring normal-width cables to form a connection instead."
		""
		"All cables can also be crafted with dye to colour them. Uncoloured (\"Fluix\") cables can connect to any other colour of cable, but otherwise differently-coloured cables will never connect to one another."
	]
	quest.5C22E3103544B120.title: "Basic Cabling"
	quest.5C4A15D3DABBA9EB.title: "Pressurized Reaction Chamber, for Sulfur!"
	quest.5CD8D169181C7339.quest_desc: [
		"These last three items are more or less some extra toys provided by AE2 and don't necessarily fit under any of these quest trees."
		""
		"The &bCharged Staff&f is just a simple powered staff which deals 3 hearts of damage and consumes 300AE per hit. It also uses pre-1.9 combat mechanics, meaning that you can spam-click with this like in the good old days."
		""
		"The &bEntropy Manipulator&f, when &oused&r on certain blocks in the world, will smelt them in-place, such as sand to glass and metal ores to metal ingots. If not, it will simply light a fire on the block."
		""
		"Finally, the &bMatter Cannon&f functions similarly to the Color Applicator as a dedicated cell for holding \"ammo\" items such as Matter Balls and iron/gold nuggets, which can then be fired out to deal damage to mobs or break blocks. Heavier \"ammo\", e.g. metal nuggets, will deal more damage and destroy harder blocks."
		""
		"Matter Balls in a Matter Cannon can be substituted with &bPaint Balls&f, which will apply a paint splatter effect on the face of whatever block being fired at. &bLumen Paint Balls&f are a variant of paint balls exclusively used by the Matter Cannon, whose paint splatters also give off some light once present in the world."
	]
	quest.5CD8D169181C7339.title: "The... Weapons?"
	quest.5D84A485688322A2.quest_desc: ["The &62x1 drawer&r holds &616 stacks&r in each of the option slots"]
	quest.5D84A485688322A2.quest_subtitle: "What it holds"
	quest.5DE1DAE7AECE29FF.title: "Locate an &5End City&r"
	quest.5E24012A3D9B72A1.quest_desc: [
		"Items are not the only things that can be stored in ME cells. &bME Fluid Storage Cells&f can store liquids such as water, lava and any variety of modded oils and fuels, just to give a few examples."
		""
		"Note that all storage cells, regardless of what they're designed to store, only differ in terms of their housing; both item and fluid cells use the same kind of storage component to make."
		""
		"For fluids, 1 byte equals 8 buckets (8000mb)."
	]
	quest.5E24012A3D9B72A1.title: "Fluid Storage"
	quest.5E6585F7627247E3.quest_desc: [
		"When applied as an upgrade to any supported device such as an Interface or Export Bus, the &bCrafting Card&f allows the device in question to automatically send out its own crafting requests for a required (filtered) item. Crafting CPUs can be set to respond only to these requests to prevent taking up CPUs meant for player-requested crafts."
		""
		"When the &eLevel Emitter&f is upgraded with the Crafting Card, it can be configured to emit redstone in order to directly facilitate in crafting, by emitting a signal either &owhile&r a crafting job for its given item is detected or specifically &oto&r craft the item. The latter would apply for cases where the only thing needed to make a given item is a redstone signal, without even requiring a crafting pattern."
	]
	quest.5E7E35CCAF1C88EE.quest_desc: ["The &bME Import Bus&f periodically sucks items in from whatever external storage the bus is facing. It can optionally be filtered to only take in certain items from said inventory."]
	quest.5F32996C76023601.title: "Energy Storage Upgrade I"
	quest.5F56892CD904C40F.quest_desc: ["The fifth and final AE2-standard tier of storage component, providing &e262144&f bytes of storage."]
	quest.5F56892CD904C40F.title: "256k Storage Component"
	quest.5F76B9E5B1861B52.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 5"
	quest.60022E0F31B7FE86.quest_subtitle: "the small connector with light can connect up to 4 wires. this connector glows when supplied with power"
	quest.608A74EE3C04347E.quest_desc: ["The &6spout&r can be used to drop liquid onto an item that's below it on a depot or belt to be able to change what the item is"]
	quest.608A74EE3C04347E.quest_subtitle: "Liquid used in crafting?"
	quest.609FC1AA946FCE5A.quest_subtitle: "Make an axe"
	quest.609FC1AA946FCE5A.title: "Becoming a lumberjack"
	quest.613FD79FA08971E6.quest_desc: ["This device provides tracking of your absorbed radiation."]
	quest.613FD79FA08971E6.title: "Dosimeter"
	quest.6144202A97C6CD1C.quest_desc: [
		"The &bQuartz Cutting Knife&f, like the wrench, comes in both nether and certus quartz flavours and is a useful crafting tool to have on hand."
		""
		"Cables can also be separated without needing to be coloured by attaching a &bCable Anchor&f between them, crafted using this knife and craftable up to 50 times with the same knife before it breaks."
		""
		"Cable Anchors can also be used to craft &bCable Facades&f, allowing you to disguise cables within walls by covering them with the face of an arbitrary block. While facade recipes are hidden in JEI, you can still craft them by taking any regular block and surrounding it with 4 cable anchors in the crafting grid."
		""
		"Aside from crafting anchors, the cutting knife also has another use: right-clicking with the knife will open a small GUI that allows you craft &bInscriber Name Presses&f. When given a name, these presses can be used inside of an Inscriber to rename any input item with the name of the press. Two of these presses can be concatenated in the inscriber to rename the item to the name of the top press, followed by the bottom one."
	]
	quest.6144202A97C6CD1C.title: "Cable Anchor"
	quest.61B3B50BE9D0A6E5.quest_subtitle: "Reduces the total stack size to 1 stack "
	quest.61E673EF387309D1.title: "Rotary Condensentrator, for Water Vapor!"
	quest.624567A93EAEFEFE.title: "Chemical Dissolution Chamber, for Hydrofluoric Acid!"
	quest.62DE24AD061AC90F.title: "Visit a &dNether Fortress&r"
	quest.6349E72C9B14CFDD.quest_subtitle: "combines items to make new items"
	quest.6358A145E9CDFDDA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6draw controller&r is the main item you will want to use to automatically put your items into drawers that are linked to the controller."
		""
		"It has a range of 12 blocks from each side, a &625x25x25&r cube with the controller as the middle block."
	]
	quest.6358A145E9CDFDDA.quest_subtitle: "The brains of storage drawers"
	quest.6431A384DDFBF439.quest_desc: [
		"The &bNetwork Tool&f is an important tool throughout AE2, which is used to display various details of a network on-screen such as overall power consumption and storage."
		""
		"As an added bonus, it also provides its own small inventory used to hold &eupgrade cards&f, which can be accessed when looking at any upgradeable device's screen for easy replacement. However, it cannot rotate blocks attached to the ME network like a regular wrench, only dismantle them when sneaking."
	]
	quest.6431A384DDFBF439.quest_subtitle: "networking"
	quest.6553CDC45C522E7F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6mixer&r has many different recipes that it can be used for."
		""
		"One of the recipes is it can make &6andesite alloy&r in a more efficient manner only costing 1 andesite and 1 iron/zinc nugget"
	]
	quest.6553CDC45C522E7F.quest_subtitle: "It's got a lot of uses"
	quest.6553CDC45C522E7F.title: "Mechanical Mixer and Basin"
	quest.657FE1419444750E.title: "Locate &5The Stronghold&r"
	quest.6710E7A154E26212.quest_subtitle: "item movement"
	quest.67528454B2FCF9D4.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 3"
	quest.68B0B3DAF1145191.quest_desc: [
		"Two of the very first things you will need to get started in AE2 are the &bCharger&f and the &bInscriber&f."
		""
		"The &bCharger&f, when supplied with power, will take &eCertus Quartz Crystals&r and charge them. These &eCharged Certus Crystals&r can then be used in the production of &eFluix&f, another important resource in the mod. It can also be used to charge any item that stores power."
		""
		"The &bInscriber&f can be used to turn the various quartz crystals in AE2 into their dust form, but more importantly is used to fabricate special &ePrinted Circuits&f and &eProcessors&f, as will become clearer in the next quest."
	]
	quest.68B0B3DAF1145191.quest_subtitle: "basic machines"
	quest.68B0B3DAF1145191.title: "First Things First"
	quest.695A48FD1A51C09E.title: "Kill the &6Warden&r"
	quest.6998C7AA5BF5E1D2.title: "Energy Storage Upgrade II"
	quest.69B1D4299D3BD075.title: "Chemical Oxidizer, for Uranium Oxide!"
	quest.69B7DE2283B4EE6C.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCrafting Co-Processing Unit&f helps speed up crafting jobs by allowing pattern providers to either send items out to their connected devices faster or to work concurrently to make multiple required ingredients."
		""
		"The base AE2 co-processor provides one co-processor \"thread\" to assist this."
	]
	quest.6A2DAD8FEB73DF63.quest_subtitle: "unlike the small connectors the large connector can connect with 6 wires"
	quest.6B17C860165713BB.title: "Electrolytic Separator, for Oxygen!"
	quest.6B3FCFFD367945DB.quest_subtitle: "Adds a bar on the drawer to show how full it is"
	quest.6B894F0707B3E19A.quest_subtitle: "The key to show or hide labels"
	quest.6BED73CFCC9342BD.quest_subtitle: "biomass is made with 100mb of seed oil and 2 of any organic material in a heated mixer. can also be compacted into pellets and water"
	quest.6C49002B17040829.title: "Energy Storage Upgrade III"
	quest.6D54B45CDA70FEAB.quest_desc: ["The &bEnergy Card&f can be applied to most chargeable devices like Portable Cells and Wireless Terminals (covered later) to also increase &otheir&r energy buffer."]
	quest.6D54B45CDA70FEAB.quest_subtitle: "more energy"
	quest.6D8322083F35B581.quest_desc: ["The &6pipe&r and &6mechanical pump&r are used hand in hand to move liquids around, the &6pump&r does need to be given so rotational speed, depending on the way the rotation goes decideds which way by default the &6pump&r wants to move the liquid, the wrench can be used on it to switch the way the liquid is moved by the pump"]
	quest.6D8322083F35B581.quest_subtitle: "Moving liquid in pipes"
	quest.6E15447FC3D678E0.quest_desc: ["The &bFuzzy Card&f allows a filtered item to be matched regardless of any (NBT) metadata such as damage or enchantments, while the &bInverter Card&f toggles the filter on such buses from being a whitelist to being a blacklist."]
	quest.6E15447FC3D678E0.title: "Fuzzy Card and Inverter Card"
	quest.6E1DCAFE1A9CE229.quest_desc: ["&6Shafts&r are way to transfer a rotation in a straight line either vertical or horizontal"]
	quest.6E1DCAFE1A9CE229.quest_subtitle: "Crafted with 2 andesite alloy"
	quest.6E1DCAFE1A9CE229.title: "Make a shaft"
	quest.6EC36AB84D09EEEA.quest_subtitle: "fuel source for the bio-generator"
	quest.6F3D0A248B5A9CA2.quest_desc: [
		"&bSpatial Storage Cells&f are used to hold one defined volume each, and come in three different capacities allowing for a maximum of 2x2x2, 16x16x16 and 128x128x128 blocks' worth of space."
		""
		"Upon encoding, a cell is allocated a section of space within the spatial storage &edimension&f, along with a unique ID corresponding to the region allocated to the cell. An encoded cell can still be used within the Spatial IO Port to retrieve any stored blocks and entities."
		""
		"From then on, any blocks contained either within the cell's region of space or in an SCS with the same size as the one used for the initial encoding can be moved back into the overworld or into the spatial dimension respectively. If there are blocks both within the spatial region and within the SCS, these will simply swap places accordingly."
	]
	quest.6F3D0A248B5A9CA2.title: "Spatial Storage"
	quest.6F4C497892554F83.quest_subtitle: "seperates the heavy water from regular water in pumps"
	quest.6FDAC276AFE8C11C.quest_desc: [
		"To speed up cogwheels you can place a &dlarge cogwheel&r adjacent to a &6small cogwheel&r"
		""
		"Then place a &dlarge cogwheel&r on the face of a &6small cogwheel&r"
		""
		"Then repeat the process as much as you can with the stress units you have available"
	]
	quest.6FDAC276AFE8C11C.quest_subtitle: " "
	quest.6FDD8A97C9F5E461.quest_desc: [
		"The &6drawer controller slave&r is kind of like the &eregular drawer controller&r but it needs a &edrawer controller&r within 12 blocks to work."
		""
		"It can be used as a secondary input for your drawer system, it's helpful if you need to have your &eregular drawer controller&r is a place that is not directly accessible to the player"
	]
	quest.6FDD8A97C9F5E461.quest_subtitle: "The wannnabe brain of storage drawers"
	quest.6FE386C83D27FF6F.quest_subtitle: "Make a wooden pickaxe"
	quest.6FE386C83D27FF6F.title: "Start your mining adventures"
	quest.6FF933A5EB730FBA.title: "Upgrade your pickaxe"
	quest.7030C384A4B63620.quest_subtitle: "uses the power of the sun to produce energy"
	quest.712061396F47312F.title: "Stack Upgrade Tier 4"
	quest.71FB9546B1E7FF13.quest_desc: [
		"The &6mechanical saw&r lets you chop down a whole tree with only destroying one of the logs using the saw."
		""
		"It can also be used to process different wooden resources, just make sure that the saw is moving in the same direction as the items are flowing"
	]
	quest.71FB9546B1E7FF13.quest_subtitle: "Advanced Lumberjacking"
	quest.71FB9546B1E7FF13.title: "Mechanical Saw"
	quest.72134A307594EA5E.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.72134A307594EA5E.quest_subtitle: "The construction of the Induction Matrix requires a bit of Lithium. This is a two-stage process using two Thermal Evaporation Plants"
	quest.72134A307594EA5E.title: "Lithium Production"
	quest.726B1D91D9DFC698.quest_subtitle: "Gives a redstone signal based on most full slot"
	quest.72CFA89AAD7EC0A6.title: "Explore the outer end"
	quest.73777D7B0F064D10.quest_subtitle: "uses bio fuel material to make energy"
	quest.7381743042291792.quest_subtitle: "keeps unwanted foes out!"
